Fixed. Changed `formatMoney()` to handle negatives by checking sign first, then formatting absolute value with appropriate prefix:

```javascript
function formatMoney(cents) {
  const isNegative = cents < 0;
  const amount = Math.abs(cents / 100).toFixed(2);
  return isNegative ? '-$' + amount : '$' + amount;
}
```

Now renders: `-$4.50` instead of `$-4.50` ✓
